# 7. ALERT ENGINE

Implement a real alert service.

Rules:

- 0–79%: normal.
- 80–94%: warning.
- 95–99%: critical.
- 100%: full.

Create an alert when the bin crosses 80%.

Avoid creating a new alert for every reading while the bin remains above the threshold.

Support:
- Acknowledging an alert.
- Resolving an alert.
- Recording who acknowledged it.
- Recording when it was resolved.
- Reopening an alert if the bin is emptied and later reaches the threshold again.

Device offline detection:

- Make the expected reporting interval configurable.
- Mark the device OFFLINE if no valid reading arrives within the configured timeout.
- Show the last successful communication time.
- Do not confuse a device with no readings yet with a device that has recently gone offline.

When the bin is emptied:
- Detect or allow staff to record the emptying event.
- Record the action and time.
- Update the bin state only when supported by a valid reading or an authorized manual operation.
- Preserve historical readings.

